how AWS offers different compute options depending on your use case, scalability needs, and operational preferences:

EC2 (IaaS) – Full control over VMs, best suited for those who want deep infrastructure management. Offers high flexibility and customization.

ECS (CaaS) – Container orchestration service that simplifies container deployment using EC2 or Fargate as launch types.

Fargate (PaaS) – Run containers without managing servers. Just define your app and let AWS handle the infrastructure!

Lambda (FaaS) – Serverless execution for short-lived, event-driven functions. Perfect for microservices and automation.
This layered approach lets you choose what level of abstraction you want:

Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)
Containers as a Service (CaaS)
Platform as a Service (PaaS)
Function as a Service (FaaS)

Choose the right compute engine based on control, scalability, and cost!
